 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? The seat height is usually set at the highest point when your leg is fully extended without bending your knee too much. If your leg is straight when your foot is at the bottom of the pedal stroke, that's good. If your knees hit the handlebars, it's too low. You were saying your bike's seat height when you' not pushing hard. Try sitting on the saddle with your feet flat on the floor. Then it' too low. Keep adjusting it until your leg's fully extended at the bottom of the pedal stroke. Most adult bikes sit at about the height of a chair's armrest, which is about where a bike shop sets bikes for people to try.",
